    "question": "Madeline needs $1200 to pay rent, $400 for groceries, $200 for medical expenses, and $60 for utilities. She also wants to save $200 in case of an emergency. She makes $15 per hour at her job. How many hours will Madeline need to work this month?",
    "gold": "138",
    "answer": "Madeline needs 1200+400+200+60+200 = $<<1200+400+200+60+200=2060>>2060 to pay all of her bills.\nShe will need to work $2060/$15 per hour = 137.33 hours.\nShe will need to work 138 hours to pay all of her bills\n#### 138"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many hours Madeline needs to work this month, we first need to calculate her total expenses and savings. Then, we will subtract her total expenses from her total income to find out how much she needs to earn in additional hours.\n\n1. Calculate Madeline's total expenses:\n   - Rent: $1200\n   - Groceries: $400\n   - Medical expenses: $200\n   - Utilities: $60\n   - Emergency savings: $200\n\n   Adding these amounts together:\n   \\[\n   1200 + 400 + 200 + 60 + 200 = 2060\n   \\]\n\n2. Determine how much more money Madeline needs to work to cover her expenses:\n   \\[\n   2060 - 200 = 1860\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate the number of hours Madeline needs to work to earn $1860, given that she makes $15 per hour:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{1860}{15} = 124\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Madeline will need to work \\(\\boxed{124}\\) hours this month.",
